---
import fs from "node:fs";
import yaml from "js-yaml";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { pi, counts } from "../lib/people.js";

const site = yaml.load(fs.readFileSync("./src/data/site.yml", "utf8"));
const isTodo = (v) =>
  typeof v === "string" && v.trim().toUpperCase().startsWith("TODO");
const { openings } = site;
---

<Base
  title="Join us"
  description="Funded graduate positions in water treatment and water chemistry at the University of Manitoba."
>
  <section class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="label">Join us</span>
      <h1>
        {openings.open ? "We are hiring graduate students" : "Openings"}
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This page tells you what is available, what we look for, and what to
        put in a first email. Reading it before you write will help both of us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <hr class="decay-rule" />
        <h2>Open positions</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        {
          openings.open ? (
            <ul class="plain roles">
              {openings.positions.map((role) => (
                <li>
                  <h3>{role.level}</h3>
                  <p class="roles__topic">{role.topic}</p>
                  <p class="roles__meta data">
                    {role.funded ? "Funded position" : "Funding to be discussed"}
                    {!isTodo(role.start) && role.start ? ` · Starting ${role.start}` : ""}
                  </p>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          ) : (
            <p>
              No positions are open at the moment. This page is kept current,
              so if nothing is listed here, nothing is available.
            </p>
          )
        }
        <p class="roles__bg">
          <strong>Useful background:</strong> {openings.background} Laboratory
          experience helps. So does programming — several projects in the group
          are as much computational as experimental.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--sunk">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <hr class="decay-rule" />
        <h2>Funding and equipment</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Graduate positions in the group are funded. The lab is supported by
          an NSERC Discovery grant running to 2028, along with project funding
          from Environment and Climate Change Canada, Research Manitoba, and
          the Water Research Foundation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Equipment matters as much as stipend. A triple quadrupole LC-MS/MS
          was installed in 2025 through the Canada Foundation for Innovation,
          which means micropollutant quantification happens in our own lab
          rather than in a queue somewhere else. See the
          <a href="/facilities">facilities page</a> for the rest.
        </p>
        <p>
          Strong applicants are also nominated for the University of Manitoba
          Graduate Fellowship. Undergraduate researchers in the group have been
          funded through NSERC and Mitacs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <hr class="decay-rule" />
        <h2>What to put in a first email</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Most of the messages we receive are sent to fifty labs at once, and
          they are easy to spot. A short, specific email gets a real reply.
          Include:
        </p>
        <ol class="asks">
          {openings.email_expectations.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ol>
        <p class="asks__addr">
          Send it to <a href={`mailto:${pi.email}`}>{pi.email}</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="asks__note">
          You will also need to meet the admission requirements of the UM
          Faculty of Graduate Studies, including the English language
          requirement. Emailing first is worth doing before you pay an
          application fee.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <hr class="decay-rule" />
        <h2>What it is like here</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          This is a young group. The lab opened at the end of 2021, and
          {" "}{counts.total} people have worked in it since. That has
          consequences worth knowing before you apply, in both directions.
        </p>
        <p>
          You will get more of your supervisor's time than you would in a large
          established group, and more say in where your project goes. Several
          of the tools the group uses were built by students. If you want to
          arrive somewhere with the questions already settled and the methods
          already working, this is the wrong lab. If you would rather help
          decide what the questions are, it is a good one.
        </p>
        <p>
          Students here are co-advised across three departments, so you are not
          dependent on a single supervisor. The group is international, and has
          been since it started.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--sunk">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <hr class="decay-rule" />
        <h2>Undergraduates</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          We take undergraduate researchers most summers, funded through NSERC
          Undergraduate Student Research Awards and Mitacs. If you are a UM
          undergraduate in engineering or a related science and want to try
          research before committing to graduate school, email in the winter
          term — awards are decided early.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .pagehead {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }
  .roles li {
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .roles li:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .roles h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .roles__topic {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .roles__meta {
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--mb-700);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .roles__bg {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--ink-70);
  }
  .asks {
    counter-reset: ask;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .asks li {
    counter-increment: ask;
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 2.4rem;
    padding-block: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .asks li::before {
    content: counter(ask);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.85rem;
    font-family: var(--data);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--mb-500);
  }
  .asks__addr {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .asks__note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink-45);
  }
</style>
